  "vibe": "Eleven at night to four in the morning, in blackened plum (#1a1216), chili red (#e63946), noodle yellow and a jade green, with condensed Kanit and titles that flip in like a menu board turning over. The world is a working counter: three steam plumes climb 800px from the base and thin out as they go, three noodle waves scroll leftward at three different depths and opacities, three hanging menu panels rock ±5° with the middle one lit chili, and a jade chopstick pair leans in from the right edge. Statement beats flood full chili; the last card goes noodle yellow with dark type. The camera drifts vertically — steam logic — under a gentle 0.7° roll. Mechanics: a menu-board scroll, a handwritten chef's note that types itself, a broth-remaining ring and a flip-to-choose swipe. Best for late-night food, bars and street markets.",
